[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Integrating Tailwind CSS with React, Vue, Svelte, and Framework Meta-tools"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Tailwind CSS is a utility-first CSS framework that can be integrated seamlessly into modern frontend frameworks and meta-frameworks. This tutorial covers setup and best practices for React, Vue, Svelte, Next.js, Nuxt, and SvelteKit."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"1. Integrating with React and Vite"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To set up Tailwind CSS in a Vite-powered React application, install Tailwind and its peer dependencies via npm."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Configure your template paths in the generated tailwind.config.js file to point to all of your source files."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./index.html",
    "./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Add the Tailwind directives to your main CSS file, typically src/index.css."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;"},{"order":10,"type":"heading","text":"2. Integrating with Vue and Vite"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Setting up Tailwind in a Vue 3 project follows a very similar pattern. Install the required packages:"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Update your tailwind.config.js content array to include Vue single-file components."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./index.html",
    "./src/**/*.{vue,js,ts,jsx,tsx}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}"},{"order":15,"heading":"heading","type":"heading","text":"3. Integrating with Svelte and SvelteKit"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"For Svelte projects, especially when utilizing SvelteKit, install Tailwind CSS and the necessary postcss dependencies."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"npm install -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Ensure your content paths cover Svelte files (.svelte) alongside JS and TS files."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"module.exports = {
  content: [
    "./src/**/*.{html,js,svelte,ts}",
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  plugins: [],
}"},{"order":20,"type":"heading","text":"4. Framework Meta-tools (Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit)"},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Next.js: Use the official Tailwind CSS guide for Next.js which automates configuration via create-next-app or manual PostCSS setups."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Nuxt 3: Install the official @nuxtjs/tailwindcss module and add it to the modules array in nuxt.config.ts for zero-config integration."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"SvelteKit: Import the global stylesheet containing @tailwind directives inside your root layout component."},{"order":24,"type":"heading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":25,"type":"paragraph","text":"By correctly configuring the content paths in tailwind.config.js and injecting the base directives into your main stylesheets, Tailwind CSS integrates natively and efficiently with React, Vue, Svelte, and their respective meta-frameworks."}]
